commit d5bb4436c7db5ea885274585d89350bddfed2518
Author: cracki <cracki@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 15:02:32 2026 +0330

    fix(qa4-P0): break refresh-401 deadlock; network-first SW; single-flight initAuth
    
    CRITICAL: after page refresh the panel went black. Root causes, all fixed:
    - client.ts: the refresh request itself was not excluded from the 401
      interceptor, so a 401 from /auth/token/refresh/ re-entered the
      interceptor which awaited its own still-pending refreshPromise
      (circular await) - logout/redirect never ran. A 401 on the refresh
      endpoint now logs out + redirects immediately (client.ts:14-24,41-72).
    - store.ts: refreshAccessToken/initAuth share a module-level
      single-flight guard so concurrent initAuth + API 401 refreshes issue
      ONE refresh call (backend rotates+blacklists refresh tokens, so a
      second concurrent call always 401'd) (store.ts:44-55,88-124).
    - sw.js: no longer precaches '/'+'index.html' (CACHE_NAME hdm-v1.1.0);
      navigations are network-first so /login can never serve a stale black
      shell; cache-first kept for static assets.
    - Backend side: REFRESH_TOKEN_LIFETIME 1d->7d (ad_creator commit
      d1d7c39).
    - client.test.ts (3) + store.test.ts (3): deadlock settlement, single
      refresh per reload, logout+redirect paths.

